<section class="sp-card"><h1>Your admission journey</h1><ol><li>Browse a course opened by your institute. Read eligibility, fee information and its privacy notice.</li><li>Verify your own email with a one-time code.</li><li>Submit accurate contact and qualification details. Keep your application reference.</li><li>Upload certificates from your application page when enabled. Uploads are quarantined until scanned and verified.</li><li>Return to My applications to track review and respond to correction requests. Status updates are queued for email, but this page is authoritative.</li><li>The office verifies eligibility and original documents before approving or rejecting admission. Some courses use owner-authorized automatic checks after certificate verification.</li><li>After approval, sign in to the enrolled-student portal for your admission letter, payments, installments, attendance, published results, notices and support.</li></ol><h2>Before you apply</h2><p>There is no guaranteed seat. Payments are collected only after admission through the enrolled-student portal, never on this application page. Contact the institute using the phone on its course page. Do not send government ID numbers, medical records, card details, passwords or OTPs in application notes.</p><h2>Already enrolled?</h2><p><a href="student.php">Use the student portal</a>. If access is disabled or your email is incorrect, contact the office. Applying again does not repair an existing student account.</p><h2>Email and privacy</h2><p>Use a personal email you control, not a shared family address. One active application per applicant is supported. An email cannot be used to create multiple student portal enrolments. Minors should contact the office about its guardian-consent process. Check the institute notice for privacy and retention information.</p></section>
